  "summary": "Flock Safety confirmed it mistakenly removed six license plate reader cameras in Lebanon, Ohio, after flagging them as inactive \u2014 the cameras had been covered since September when the city council paused the program over data-practice concerns. Earlier in October the council voted 4-3 against terminating the Flock contract, opting to keep cameras in place but covered during ongoing review.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The cameras were removed in error, and Flock is working with the customer to determine the appropriate next steps",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "Lebanon City Council voted 4-3 earlier this month against terminating its contract with Flock Safety.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "We believe at this point there is nothing nefarious with the removal of some of our Flock cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    }
  ],
